From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Share the wire of a redefined net

A redefinition (output q; wire q, q;), which slang accepts with
-Wredefinition, got a wire of its own that took the port wire's name,
and with --keep-hierarchy the module lost the port:

  ERROR: Module `controller$top.controller_i' referenced in module
  `top' in cell `controller_i' does not have a port named 'q'.

The redefinition now shares the wire of the symbol name lookup finds.
---
 src/slang_frontend.cc | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/slang_frontend.cc b/src/slang_frontend.cc
index b51ddb0..74a97bf 100644
--- a/src/slang_frontend.cc
+++ b/src/slang_frontend.cc
@@ -3140,6 +3140,21 @@ bool is_special_net(const ast::Symbol &symbol)
 
 const RTLIL::SigSpec& NetlistContext::add_wire(const ast::ValueSymbol &symbol)
 {
+	// A redefinition (`output q; wire q, q;`, accepted with
+	// -Wredefinition) is not a second net: it shares the wire of the
+	// symbol name lookup finds. A wire of its own took the name of the
+	// port's wire, and with --keep-hierarchy the module lost the port.
+	if (const ast::Scope *scope = symbol.getParentScope()) {
+		const ast::Symbol *found = scope->find(symbol.name);
+		if (found && found != &symbol && ast::ValueSymbol::isKind(found->kind)) {
+			auto it = wire_cache.find(found);
+			RTLIL::SigSpec sig = it != wire_cache.end()
+					? it->second : add_wire(found->as<ast::ValueSymbol>());
+			wire_cache[&symbol] = sig;
+			return wire_cache[&symbol];
+		}
+	}
+
 	auto &type = symbol.getType();
 
 	AttributeGuard guard(*this);
